<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">François Tomb</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">4th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The François Tomb is an Etruscan chamber tomb at Vulci, discovered in 1857 by Alessandro François, with wall paintings of the 4th century BCE. Its frescoes pair <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achilles">Achilles</a> sacrificing Trojan prisoners with local heroes: <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mastarna">Macstrna</a> freeing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caelius-vibenna">Caelius Vibenna</a> and Vulcian warriors killing enemies, among them a Gnaeus Tarquinius of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. The paintings are now in the Villa Albani in Rome.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/francois-tomb.jpg" alt="François Tomb" width="320" height="170" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Arch. S. Bruba ? · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tomba_di_Francois_a_Vulci.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
